<title>USA: McDonald's files $1 bln debt shelf.</title>
<headline>McDonald's files $1 bln debt shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>McDonald's Corp said Tuesday it filed a shelf registration with the Securities and Exchange Commission for up to $1 billion in debt securities.</p>
<p>The fast-food giant based in Oak brook, Ill., said net proceeds from the sale of the securities will be used for general corporate purposes, which may include refinancing of debt capital expenditures and development of restaurants.</p>
</text>
